Subject: [CoordinatedGraphics] Do not invalidate every render target on a frame without damage

Draft against the webkitgtk-2.52.6 release tarball. Apply with -p1 from the
tarball root. Independent of 0001 (it only matters when
UseDamagingInformationForCompositing is on). Required by 0003. Not compiled.

What it does
  AcceleratedSurface::setFrameDamage() stores an empty frame damage as
  std::nullopt. renderTargetDamage() then handed that nullopt to
  SwapChain::addDamage(), and RenderTarget::addDamage(std::nullopt) resets the
  record of every target to "unknown". One composited frame without damage
  therefore cost a full repaint of the current target and of the next frame on
  every other target. With this change an empty frame leaves the records alone.

  A target whose record is empty is up to date. The empty bounds would send
  TextureMapper::beginClip() down the stencil path (beginScissorClip() refuses
  empty rects), so the compositor clips to a single pixel instead. The layer
  tree is still walked, nothing else is rasterized.

What it does not handle
  - A visual change that damage tracking does not report and that happens
    alone in a frame was hidden by the full repaint before, and would now be
    presented one frame late or not at all. 2.54 has the same behaviour
    (ThreadedCompositor::recordFrameDamage() returns early on empty damage).
  - The frame is still read back and sent to the UI process.

--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
@@ -1097,7 +1097,10 @@
 
 const std::optional<Damage>& AcceleratedSurface::renderTargetDamage()
 {
-    m_swapChain.addDamage(m_frameDamage);
+    // setFrameDamage() stores an empty frame damage as std::nullopt. Passing that on would reset the
+    // damage record of every target to "unknown" and make each of them repaint in full.
+    if (m_frameDamage)
+        m_swapChain.addDamage(m_frameDamage);
     static std::optional<Damage> nulloptDamage;
     return m_target ? m_target->damage() : nulloptDamage;
 }
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
@@ -292,8 +292,15 @@
 
         if (m_damage.flags->contains(DamagePropagationFlags::UseForCompositing)) {
             const auto& damageSinceLastSurfaceUse = m_surface->renderTargetDamage();
-            if (damageSinceLastSurfaceUse && !FloatRect(damageSinceLastSurfaceUse->bounds()).contains(clipRect))
-                rectContainingRegionThatActuallyChanged = FloatRoundedRect(damageSinceLastSurfaceUse->bounds());
+            if (damageSinceLastSurfaceUse) {
+                // A target with an empty damage record is up to date. TextureMapper::beginClip() takes
+                // the stencil path for an empty rect, so clip to one pixel to stay on the scissor path.
+                auto damageBounds = damageSinceLastSurfaceUse->bounds();
+                if (damageBounds.isEmpty())
+                    damageBounds = IntRect(0, 0, 1, 1);
+                if (!FloatRect(damageBounds).contains(clipRect))
+                    rectContainingRegionThatActuallyChanged = FloatRoundedRect(FloatRect(damageBounds));
+            }
 
             m_textureMapper->setDamage(damageSinceLastSurfaceUse);
         }
